<pre class=metadata>
Title: Window Focus Media Query
Shortname: window-focus-media-query
Level: none
Status: LD
ED: https://arronei.github.io/CSS-Additions/system-media-queries/window-focus/spec/
Repository: arronei/CSS-Additions
Editor: Arron Eicholz
Abstract: This specification adds the '@media/window-focus' media feature, which reports whether the
    window showing the document is the one the user is using, so web apps can dim their title bars and
    selections when the window is in the background, as native apps do. Top-level documents already learn
    this from <code>focus</code> and <code>blur</code> events, and the feature reveals no more to them.
    Cross-origin frames learn only whether they themselves have focus, unless the embedding page allows
    more, and documents without script always see an active window.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, css yes
Complain About: accidental-2119 no, missing-example-ids yes
Assume Explicit For: yes
</pre>

